1
00:00:02,410 --> 00:00:03,410
Oh, my God.

2
00:00:03,580 --> 00:00:07,000
I know. Monica's gonna have a baby.

3
00:00:07,210 --> 00:00:09,960
Can this count as her "something new"?

4
00:00:10,880 --> 00:00:12,260
Oh, my God.

5
00:00:15,930 --> 00:00:18,350
Do you think this is why Chandler took off?

6
00:00:18,600 --> 00:00:22,850
She had to have just taken it. I took out the trash last night.

7
00:00:23,060 --> 00:00:25,560
It's turning into the worst wedding ever.

8
00:00:25,770 --> 00:00:30,270
The bride's pregnant, the groom's missing and I'm holding this.

9
00:00:31,280 --> 00:00:35,950
Phoebe, we cannot tell anyone about this.

10
00:00:36,160 --> 00:00:38,200
Right. Yeah.

11
00:00:36,160 --> 00:00:38,200
Okay?

12
00:00:38,450 --> 00:00:41,870
Do you know what kind of birth control she uses?

13
00:00:42,120 --> 00:00:43,120
No. Why?

14
00:00:43,370 --> 00:00:47,370
Just for the future. This is hardly a commercial for it.

15
00:01:09,270 --> 00:01:10,270
Anything?

16
00:01:10,440 --> 00:01:13,820
No. I talked to Joey. He hasn't heard from him.

17
00:01:14,070 --> 00:01:16,650
I talked to Chandler's parents again.

18
00:01:16,860 --> 00:01:18,860
You said he was missing?

19
00:01:16,860 --> 00:01:18,860
No.

20
00:01:19,120 --> 00:01:21,240
It seemed like I called to chat.

21
00:01:21,490 --> 00:01:24,620
Pretty sure they both think I'm interested.

22
00:01:24,830 --> 00:01:27,290
We've got to tell her.

23
00:01:24,830 --> 00:01:27,290
No, we can't.

24
00:01:27,540 --> 00:01:29,790
She'll start getting ready soon.

25
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:34,300
Can't you stall her? I'll go to the places I went last night.

26
00:01:34,510 --> 00:01:35,800
How much time?

27
00:01:36,010 --> 00:01:38,720
How long before she has to get ready?

28
00:01:38,930 --> 00:01:40,470
One hour.

29
00:01:38,930 --> 00:01:40,470
Give me two.

30
00:01:40,680 --> 00:01:42,810
Then why do you ask?

31
00:01:44,180 --> 00:01:46,640
Wish me luck.

32
00:01:44,180 --> 00:01:46,640
I'm going with you.

33
00:01:46,850 --> 00:01:48,390
Why?

34
00:01:48,600 --> 00:01:52,650
You're tired. You looked all night. And clearly, you suck at this.

35
00:01:54,110 --> 00:01:55,110
See you later.

36
00:01:55,320 --> 00:01:57,070
Wait, do you know how you're gonna stall her?

37
00:01:57,280 --> 00:02:00,570
I'll figure something out.

38
00:01:57,280 --> 00:02:00,570
Okay, good luck.

39
00:02:03,200 --> 00:02:06,410
Let's start with my makeup and then do my hair.

40
00:02:06,620 --> 00:02:10,500
Okay. But before you do that, I need you to talk to me.

41
00:02:10,750 --> 00:02:12,500
About what?

42
00:02:14,710 --> 00:02:18,550
I'm never gonna get married.

43
00:02:18,760 --> 00:02:21,720
You will. The right guy's around the corner.

44
00:02:21,970 --> 00:02:24,180
Okay, are we done with that?

45
00:02:24,970 --> 00:02:26,680
No, I'm serious.

46
00:02:26,890 --> 00:02:32,150
Maybe I should just forget about it. Become a lesbian or something.

47
00:02:32,360 --> 00:02:35,360
Any woman would be lucky to have you.

48
00:02:36,900 --> 00:02:39,780
Maybe I'd feel better if I slept with Joey.

49
00:02:39,990 --> 00:02:42,910
Rachel? Are you okay?

50
00:02:45,990 --> 00:02:51,000
Excuse me, Aaron? I have a little problem with the schedule.

51
00:02:51,210 --> 00:02:56,040
I wasn't supposed to work today. I have a wedding that I have to be at.

52
00:02:56,300 --> 00:02:59,130
It's my best friend's, and I'm officiating...

53
00:02:59,340 --> 00:03:01,300
...so I really can't work past 4.

54
00:03:01,550 --> 00:03:05,800
You've gotta stay until the end. We can't stop filming just for you.

55
00:03:06,010 --> 00:03:08,770
It's not like it's your wedding.

56
00:03:08,980 --> 00:03:10,980
I'm having surgery.

57
00:03:12,190 --> 00:03:13,480
What?

58
00:03:13,690 --> 00:03:17,770
I made up the wedding, because I didn't want you to worry.

59
00:03:18,030 --> 00:03:20,150
But I'm having surgery today.

60
00:03:20,360 --> 00:03:21,990
What kind of surgery?

61
00:03:22,910 --> 00:03:25,030
Transplant.

62
00:03:26,530 --> 00:03:28,790
You're supposed to work on Monday.

63
00:03:29,290 --> 00:03:31,960
Hair transplant.

64
00:03:32,420 --> 00:03:34,500
But you're not bald.

65
00:03:34,670 --> 00:03:36,880
It's not on my head.

66
00:03:40,340 --> 00:03:45,220
There's nothing I can do. You'll probably be out by 4 anyway.

67
00:03:45,470 --> 00:03:49,890
We've got one scene. It's just you and Richard, and he's a pro.

68
00:03:50,100 --> 00:03:52,180
You'll be fine.

69
00:03:52,730 --> 00:03:54,060
Morning, Richard.

70
00:03:54,310 --> 00:03:57,310
Hey, you're here. Great. Let's go, buddy.

71
00:03:57,570 --> 00:03:59,900
We got a scene to shoot.

72
00:04:00,820 --> 00:04:04,280
I'm wearing two belts.

73
00:04:06,700 --> 00:04:09,030
Are you drunk?

74
00:04:06,700 --> 00:04:09,030
No.

75
00:04:09,240 --> 00:04:11,040
Yes, you are.

76
00:04:11,290 --> 00:04:12,830
All right.

77
00:04:16,750 --> 00:04:18,250
So this is your office?

78
00:04:18,460 --> 00:04:22,210
How'd you guys find me? I knew I should've hid at the gym.

79
00:04:23,590 --> 00:04:26,300
What the hell are you doing?

80
00:04:23,590 --> 00:04:26,300
Panicking.

81
00:04:26,510 --> 00:04:31,220
And using the Internet to try to prove that I'm related to Monica.

82
00:04:33,270 --> 00:04:36,020
How is she?

83
00:04:33,270 --> 00:04:36,020
She doesn't know you're gone.

84
00:04:36,230 --> 00:04:39,900
And she doesn't have to know. Come on, we're going home.

85
00:04:40,110 --> 00:04:42,480
I can't do that.

86
00:04:40,110 --> 00:04:42,480
Why not?

87
00:04:42,690 --> 00:04:45,860
If I go home, we're gonna become the Bings.

88
00:04:46,110 --> 00:04:47,820
I can't be the Bings.

89
00:04:48,070 --> 00:04:49,530
What's wrong with it?

90
00:04:49,740 --> 00:04:51,740
The Bings have bad marriages.

91
00:04:51,950 --> 00:04:54,660
They yell, fight, and use the pool boy...

92
00:04:54,910 --> 00:04:57,290
...as a pawn in their sexual games.

93
00:04:58,250 --> 00:05:03,090
Have you ever put on a black dress and asked me up to your hotel room?

94
00:05:03,300 --> 00:05:07,590
No.

95
00:05:03,300 --> 00:05:07,590
Then you are neither of your parents.

96
00:05:09,260 --> 00:05:13,640
It's not just their marriage. Look at yours. Look at everybody's.

97
00:05:13,850 --> 00:05:16,890
Only Paul Newman can make marriage work.

98
00:05:17,100 --> 00:05:18,980
And I am no Paul Newman.

99
00:05:19,230 --> 00:05:24,190
I don't race cars or make popcorn. None of my proceeds go to charity.

100
00:05:24,900 --> 00:05:26,280
But look, Chandler...

101
00:05:27,070 --> 00:05:31,410
...right now no one has a lower opinion of you than I do.

102
00:05:33,240 --> 00:05:35,830
But I totally believe you can do this.

103
00:05:36,410 --> 00:05:40,040
I want to. I love her so much, but I'm afraid...

104
00:05:40,210 --> 00:05:42,250
Ahem. It's too huge.

105
00:05:42,500 --> 00:05:44,500
You're right. It is huge.

106
00:05:44,760 --> 00:05:48,260
So let's take it just a little bit at a time.

107
00:05:48,510 --> 00:05:51,600
Forget getting married for a sec.

108
00:05:51,800 --> 00:05:55,810
Can you just come home and take a shower?

109
00:05:56,020 --> 00:05:58,060
That's not scary, right?

110
00:05:58,270 --> 00:06:00,850
Depends on what you mean by "we."

111
00:06:02,900 --> 00:06:05,230
The nights are the hardest.

112
00:06:07,570 --> 00:06:09,700
But then the day comes...

113
00:06:09,950 --> 00:06:14,030
...and that's every bit as hard as the night.

114
00:06:14,240 --> 00:06:18,250
Then the night comes...

115
00:06:14,240 --> 00:06:18,250
Days and nights are hard, I get it.

116
00:06:18,500 --> 00:06:22,420
I have to start getting ready. I'm getting married today.

117
00:06:22,670 --> 00:06:25,420
I know. At dusk.

118
00:06:25,630 --> 00:06:28,340
That's such a hard time for me.

119
00:06:28,880 --> 00:06:32,550
I'm gonna put makeup on. We have to be there in an hour.

120
00:06:32,800 --> 00:06:34,140
Wait.

121
00:06:32,800 --> 00:06:34,140
What?

122
00:06:34,350 --> 00:06:36,560
Let's go to lunch.

123
00:06:36,770 --> 00:06:39,020
I can't go to lunch.

124
00:06:39,270 --> 00:06:40,980
Right.

125
00:06:43,230 --> 00:06:45,440
Oh, good God, I've fallen down.

126
00:06:47,900 --> 00:06:49,820
What's going on?

127
00:06:50,530 --> 00:06:51,990
Okay.

128
00:06:52,410 --> 00:06:54,120
All right, honey, listen.

129
00:06:55,490 --> 00:06:59,910
When I tell you what I'm about to tell you, remember...

130
00:07:00,160 --> 00:07:03,710
...that we're all here for you, and we love you.

131
00:07:03,920 --> 00:07:06,130
Okay, you're really freaking me out.

132
00:07:08,130 --> 00:07:10,470
We can't find Chandler...

133
00:07:11,760 --> 00:07:13,390
His vest.

134
00:07:14,140 --> 00:07:16,260
We can't find Chandler's vest.

135
00:07:16,470 --> 00:07:18,560
How can that be? Wait, are you serious?

136
00:07:20,890 --> 00:07:22,060
Found the vest.

137
00:07:22,270 --> 00:07:25,610
We'll have to keep an eye on it, make sure we don't lose it again.

138
00:07:26,020 --> 00:07:27,230
Ah.

139
00:07:27,400 --> 00:07:31,110
Oh, wow. Okay, don't scare me like that, okay?

140
00:07:31,320 --> 00:07:35,780
For a minute, I was like, "Oh, my God. The worst has happened."

141
00:07:49,880 --> 00:07:51,720
So you two were married, huh?

142
00:07:53,890 --> 00:07:56,390
What happened, you just drift apart?

143
00:07:58,100 --> 00:08:00,770
Here comes the bride.

144
00:08:02,980 --> 00:08:06,440
Oh, my God, Monica.

145
00:08:06,860 --> 00:08:09,440
I want to wear this every day.

146
00:08:09,650 --> 00:08:11,690
You look so beautiful.

147
00:08:12,990 --> 00:08:14,780
I'm so happy for me.

148
00:08:18,830 --> 00:08:21,870
Hello?

149
00:08:18,830 --> 00:08:21,870
Did Chandler show up yet?

150
00:08:22,080 --> 00:08:25,580
We got him back. Everything's fine.

151
00:08:22,080 --> 00:08:25,580
Damn it.

152
00:08:25,790 --> 00:08:28,340
Where are you?

153
00:08:25,790 --> 00:08:28,340
I'm still on the set.

154
00:08:28,540 --> 00:08:31,630
The wedding is in less than an hour.

155
00:08:31,840 --> 00:08:36,640
I'm sorry. The guy's drunk. They won't let me go until we get it.

156
00:08:36,840 --> 00:08:40,430
Oh, my God. I'm gonna have to find another minister.

157
00:08:40,640 --> 00:08:43,270
No, I'm the minister.

158
00:08:43,520 --> 00:08:47,600
Put them both on the phone and I'll marry them right now.

159
00:08:47,860 --> 00:08:49,230
Joey, I have to go.

160
00:08:49,440 --> 00:08:53,110
Don't hang up on me. I'll marry you and me right now. I have the power.

161
00:08:57,280 --> 00:09:00,490
There you go. You put on a tuxedo.

162
00:09:01,200 --> 00:09:03,120
That wasn't scary, was it?

163
00:09:03,830 --> 00:09:05,660
No.

164
00:09:05,870 --> 00:09:08,920
I'm telling you, just a little bit at a time.

165
00:09:09,420 --> 00:09:12,170
Okay. What's the next little bit?

166
00:09:12,420 --> 00:09:14,420
Getting married.

167
00:09:12,420 --> 00:09:14,420
Oh, ah.

168
00:09:14,630 --> 00:09:19,550
You can do that too. Just like you've done everything else.

169
00:09:21,390 --> 00:09:25,310
Yeah, you're right. I can do that.

170
00:09:21,390 --> 00:09:25,310
Yeah.

171
00:09:25,480 --> 00:09:29,270
Excuse me for a minute.

172
00:09:25,480 --> 00:09:29,270
Where you going?

173
00:09:29,520 --> 00:09:33,110
I'm not gonna run away. I just want some fresh air.

174
00:09:33,650 --> 00:09:35,690
Okay.

175
00:09:33,650 --> 00:09:35,690
Okay.

176
00:09:44,200 --> 00:09:46,750
Oh, fresh air.

177
00:09:48,580 --> 00:09:52,710
Cover for me.

178
00:09:48,580 --> 00:09:52,710
Maybe you overreacted.

179
00:09:52,960 --> 00:09:54,710
We gotta do something.

180
00:09:54,960 --> 00:09:59,510
Joey won't make it, so I'll look around for other weddings.

181
00:09:59,760 --> 00:10:04,260
Don't tell them Monica's pregnant, because they frown on that.

182
00:10:04,430 --> 00:10:05,770
Okay.

183
00:10:16,990 --> 00:10:21,570
"Anastassakis Papasifakis wedding." Excellent.

184
00:10:23,490 --> 00:10:25,410
Congratulations.

185
00:10:25,660 --> 00:10:27,580
Mazel tov.

186
00:10:27,830 --> 00:10:29,790
Hi. Oh, great hat.

187
00:10:31,130 --> 00:10:34,920
I need you to perform another wedding. Can you do that?

188
00:10:35,130 --> 00:10:38,050
I don't know. Are they Greek Orthodox?

189
00:10:38,260 --> 00:10:39,840
Yeah. Yeah.

190
00:10:40,090 --> 00:10:44,600
They're my friends, Monica Stephanopolis.

191
00:10:44,850 --> 00:10:49,100
And Chandler Acidophilus.

192
00:10:53,440 --> 00:10:56,190
Hi. Hi.

193
00:10:57,740 --> 00:10:58,940
Hi.

194
00:11:02,070 --> 00:11:04,030
Has anyone seen Chandler?

195
00:11:04,240 --> 00:11:07,240
I thought he was with you.

196
00:11:04,240 --> 00:11:07,240
He was with me.

197
00:11:07,500 --> 00:11:10,210
We're playing a game. Hide-and-seek.

198
00:11:10,410 --> 00:11:13,290
You can't ask us, son. That's cheating.

199
00:11:18,130 --> 00:11:21,800
You're right. Thanks for keeping me honest, Dad.

200
00:11:22,010 --> 00:11:25,800
He can't come here and see the bride in her wedding dress.

201
00:11:26,010 --> 00:11:30,310
When we got married, I saw the groom in the wedding dress.

202
00:11:31,270 --> 00:11:34,650
That was after the wedding. It's not bad luck then.

203
00:11:34,860 --> 00:11:37,020
Honey, it isn't good luck.

204
00:11:41,360 --> 00:11:44,490
Oh, my God. Monica.

205
00:11:44,700 --> 00:11:46,450
I know.

206
00:11:47,490 --> 00:11:50,910
How's Chandler doing?

207
00:11:47,490 --> 00:11:50,910
Great.

208
00:11:51,120 --> 00:11:54,920
He's doing great. Don't you worry about Chandler.

209
00:11:56,500 --> 00:12:00,000
Phoebe, can I see you for a second?

210
00:11:56,500 --> 00:12:00,000
Yeah.

211
00:12:05,430 --> 00:12:07,800
What's going on?

212
00:12:05,430 --> 00:12:07,800
Chandler's gone again.

213
00:12:08,060 --> 00:12:13,480
Why would you play hide-and-seek with someone you know is a flight risk?

214
00:12:17,440 --> 00:12:20,980
Aaron, you gotta let me go. The guy's hammered.

215
00:12:21,190 --> 00:12:26,110
I'm sorry. As long as he's here and conscious, we're still shooting.

216
00:12:35,330 --> 00:12:39,250
You wouldn't happen to have a very big fork?

217
00:12:40,840 --> 00:12:43,550
So I just talked to the director.

218
00:12:43,760 --> 00:12:46,590
That's it. We're done for the day.

219
00:12:47,550 --> 00:12:49,180
We finished the scene?

220
00:12:49,430 --> 00:12:54,060
Yeah. You were wonderful.

221
00:12:49,430 --> 00:12:54,060
As were you.

222
00:12:54,890 --> 00:12:57,020
So I got your car. It's right outside.

223
00:12:57,230 --> 00:12:59,770
Thank you. You're welcome.

224
00:13:00,570 --> 00:13:04,570
No, we gotta go. Come on. Here we go.

225
00:13:06,070 --> 00:13:08,320
Is that my ass?

226
00:13:15,460 --> 00:13:17,330
There he is!

227
00:13:15,460 --> 00:13:17,330
What?

228
00:13:18,130 --> 00:13:19,330
Hey! Whoa!

229
00:13:20,090 --> 00:13:22,170
You won't get away this time!

230
00:13:22,380 --> 00:13:25,550
Unless you want that ass-kicking we talked about.

231
00:13:26,760 --> 00:13:29,050
Ross.

232
00:13:26,760 --> 00:13:29,050
Hi-yah!

233
00:13:31,140 --> 00:13:34,810
I'm serious. You're not walking out on my sister.

234
00:13:35,020 --> 00:13:36,730
That's right. I'm not.

235
00:13:36,980 --> 00:13:40,610
Then where have you been?

236
00:13:36,980 --> 00:13:40,610
I know about Monica.

237
00:13:41,730 --> 00:13:43,780
You know?

238
00:13:41,730 --> 00:13:43,780
What?

239
00:13:43,980 --> 00:13:47,280
I heard you and Rachel talking.

240
00:13:43,980 --> 00:13:47,280
About what?

241
00:13:47,490 --> 00:13:48,610
You don't know?

242
00:13:48,820 --> 00:13:52,200
If somebody doesn't tell me right now...

243
00:13:52,410 --> 00:13:54,200
What, you'll "hi-yah"?

244
00:13:56,250 --> 00:13:58,080
Monica's pregnant.

245
00:13:59,920 --> 00:14:01,750
Oh, my God.

246
00:14:02,000 --> 00:14:05,630
Oh, my God. And you're not freaking out?

247
00:14:05,840 --> 00:14:09,800
I was. Then I went to the gift shop for cigarettes.

248
00:14:10,010 --> 00:14:13,300
Cigarettes?

249
00:14:10,010 --> 00:14:13,300
Big picture, please.

250
00:14:14,850 --> 00:14:19,230
So I was in the gift shop, that's when I saw this...

251
00:14:20,940 --> 00:14:25,320
And I thought anything that can fit into this can't be scary.

252
00:14:25,900 --> 00:14:29,400
You obviously didn't see Chuckie III.

253
00:14:30,070 --> 00:14:33,450
But come on, look at how cute and small this is.

254
00:14:33,700 --> 00:14:38,450
So I got it to give Monica, so she'd know I was okay.

255
00:14:38,660 --> 00:14:40,080
Dude.

256
00:14:40,670 --> 00:14:43,630
Way to go, son. I knew you'd find him.

257
00:14:52,970 --> 00:14:55,310
Our little boy is getting married.

258
00:14:55,510 --> 00:14:58,430
Look at you, so handsome.

259
00:14:58,640 --> 00:15:00,230
You look beautiful, Mom.

260
00:15:03,860 --> 00:15:06,360
You look beautiful too, Dad.

261
00:15:09,740 --> 00:15:11,780
I love you both.

262
00:15:12,070 --> 00:15:14,070
I'm so glad you're here.

263
00:15:20,040 --> 00:15:22,080
Are you Chandler?

264
00:15:22,330 --> 00:15:24,290
Are you Joey?

265
00:15:29,130 --> 00:15:32,220
Huh. This is nice.

266
00:15:29,130 --> 00:15:32,220
What?

267
00:15:32,470 --> 00:15:37,010
I've never walked down the aisle knowing it can't end in divorce.

268
00:15:52,740 --> 00:15:56,200
I wish your grandmother had lived to see this.

269
00:15:56,410 --> 00:16:00,790
She's right there.

270
00:15:56,410 --> 00:16:00,790
Not that old crone. My mother.

271
00:16:04,290 --> 00:16:06,630
Congratulations, darling.

272
00:16:06,880 --> 00:16:08,920
We love you, sweetheart.

273
00:16:12,930 --> 00:16:14,970
You look beautiful.

274
00:16:15,720 --> 00:16:18,300
Is this new?

275
00:16:15,720 --> 00:16:18,300
Not now.

276
00:16:22,640 --> 00:16:25,140
Who's this?

277
00:16:22,640 --> 00:16:25,140
I'm Father Karabasos.

278
00:16:25,350 --> 00:16:27,150
He's Greek Orthodox.

279
00:16:27,360 --> 00:16:29,770
As are you.

280
00:16:31,940 --> 00:16:33,570
Let us begin.

281
00:16:34,700 --> 00:16:35,950
Dearly beloved...

282
00:16:36,160 --> 00:16:38,120
That's my line.

283
00:16:42,910 --> 00:16:45,500
I can take it from here. Thanks.

284
00:16:47,540 --> 00:16:51,460
Dearly beloved, I'm sorry I'm a little late.

285
00:16:54,010 --> 00:16:56,880
You may be confused by this now...

286
00:16:57,140 --> 00:17:01,060
...but you won't be Memorial Day weekend, 2002.

287
00:17:03,850 --> 00:17:07,560
Let's get started before the groom takes off again.

288
00:17:13,940 --> 00:17:16,490
We are gathered here today...

289
00:17:16,700 --> 00:17:19,200
...to join this man...

290
00:17:19,410 --> 00:17:23,790
...and this woman in the bonds of holy matrimony.

291
00:17:24,620 --> 00:17:28,830
I've known Monica and Chandler for a long time, and I can't...

292
00:17:29,080 --> 00:17:33,760
...imagine two people more perfect for each other.

293
00:17:36,260 --> 00:17:41,300
And now, as I've left my notes in my dressing room...

294
00:17:42,060 --> 00:17:45,680
...we shall proceed to the vows. Monica?

295
00:17:46,810 --> 00:17:50,060
He took off?

296
00:17:46,810 --> 00:17:50,060
Go on. Go on.

297
00:17:55,440 --> 00:17:59,450
Chandler, for so long...

298
00:17:59,870 --> 00:18:03,620
...I wondered if I would ever find my prince.

299
00:18:03,870 --> 00:18:05,790
My soul mate.

300
00:18:06,000 --> 00:18:08,830
Then three years ago, at another wedding...

301
00:18:09,080 --> 00:18:11,670
...I turned to a friend for comfort.

302
00:18:11,920 --> 00:18:17,130
And instead, I found everything that I'd been looking for my whole life.

303
00:18:19,930 --> 00:18:21,760
And now...

304
00:18:22,850 --> 00:18:24,680
...here we are...

305
00:18:25,560 --> 00:18:28,020
...with our future before us.

306
00:18:29,270 --> 00:18:31,980
And I only want to spend it with you.

307
00:18:33,320 --> 00:18:37,400
My prince. My soul mate.

308
00:18:37,610 --> 00:18:39,700
My friend.

309
00:18:42,490 --> 00:18:44,910
Unless you don't want to.

310
00:18:47,290 --> 00:18:48,870
You go.

311
00:18:50,290 --> 00:18:51,330
Chandler?

312
00:18:52,500 --> 00:18:54,710
No, that's okay.

313
00:18:58,970 --> 00:19:03,470
I thought this would be the most difficult thing I ever had to do.

314
00:19:05,010 --> 00:19:09,520
But when I saw you walking down that aisle, I realized it's simple.

315
00:19:12,150 --> 00:19:13,440
I love you.

316
00:19:15,360 --> 00:19:20,570
Any surprises that come our way, it's okay, because I will always love you.

317
00:19:22,780 --> 00:19:27,030
You are the person I was meant to spend the rest of my life with.

318
00:19:27,290 --> 00:19:29,540
You want to know if I'm sure?

319
00:19:33,040 --> 00:19:35,960
You may now kiss the bride.

320
00:19:38,010 --> 00:19:39,510
So...

321
00:19:39,670 --> 00:19:43,430
I guess by the powers vested in me by the State of New York...

322
00:19:43,680 --> 00:19:46,140
...and the Internet guys...

323
00:19:48,430 --> 00:19:52,480
...I now pronounce you husband and wife.

324
00:19:52,900 --> 00:19:55,730
Oh, wait. Do you take each other?

325
00:19:55,940 --> 00:19:58,230
I do.

326
00:19:55,940 --> 00:19:58,230
I do.

327
00:19:58,440 --> 00:20:00,030
Yeah, you do.

328
00:20:01,400 --> 00:20:02,610
Rings?

329
00:20:02,820 --> 00:20:04,570
Oh, crap.

330
00:20:06,370 --> 00:20:08,120
Let's do the rings.

331
00:20:19,340 --> 00:20:21,880
We good? Yeah? Good?

332
00:20:23,130 --> 00:20:24,840
Once again...

333
00:20:25,090 --> 00:20:28,640
...I pronounce you husband and wife.

334
00:20:28,890 --> 00:20:31,060
Now kiss her again.

335
00:20:46,240 --> 00:20:47,950
I love you.

336
00:20:48,200 --> 00:20:50,330
And I know about the baby.

337
00:20:51,200 --> 00:20:53,250
What baby?

338
00:20:51,200 --> 00:20:53,250
Our baby.

339
00:20:53,460 --> 00:20:55,210
We have a baby?

340
00:20:56,790 --> 00:20:59,210
Phoebe found your pregnancy test.

341
00:20:59,420 --> 00:21:01,590
I didn't take a pregnancy test.

342
00:21:01,800 --> 00:21:03,630
Then who did?

343
00:21:04,380 --> 00:21:06,930
Look at them.

344
00:21:07,180 --> 00:21:10,050
And they're gonna have a baby.

345
00:21:11,680 --> 00:21:13,470
Uh-huh.

